# Wisdom

## On People
- Don't be caught up in materialistic things and trying to impress the wrong people. Those people most likely won't be in your life later.
- The ones you feel will always be there are the ones that go away first. Your true friends are the ones you never realized were your friends — it doesn't matter how long since you've hung out. They will always be your friend.
- Don't allow people to take advantage of you. Learn to say no. Learn to say "I need more from you." People will do everything in their power to take full advantage of you without you realizing it, or you not being willing to speak up about it.

## On Life
- Don't take things for granted.
- Always trust your initial intuition, your gut. It is generally right.
- When things feel too good to be true, it will always come crashing down and spoil the hard work you've put in to get where you're at.
- Life is more than what's in front of your screen. Touch grass. Be around people. Build things. Use your hands. You don't know when you're going to lose all of that.
- Have the ability to think clearly without fog and have the motivation to do things without additional chemicals like caffeine. Just do.
- Don't waste time planning the rest of your life because none of that means anything. Just do the things you want.
